ere able to do i believe we counted 128  player interviews in person now we had  mask on we had plexiglass between us but  you actually got to do that in person  instead of virtual and  you know those things are important too  because a lot of things you may not see  uh virtually you can actually see body  language and things like that get a real  good feel for the person and their  personality and then just to get to see  some of these kids  that opted out in 2020 or their schools  didn't play till this spring to see a  couple of those guys go down there and  participate uh was huge for us but this  year the pro days are going to i think  be bigger than ever because of the  limitations we've had and the exposure  we've had to a lot of these uh upcoming  draft prospects so i'm excited to to  really get out out on the road and like  most of my counterparts are i'm sure uh  to see these guys see them move around  and watch them work out for the guys who  walk out or for the guys who played for  the teams that maybe didn't  play in a lot of games last season  um  how hard is it to go back to your 2019  film  and project from that it's got to be  frustrating because you want to have  apples to apples  you you don't have the full set of film  that you ordinarily would have for a lot  of these guys no and we did we knew that  there was going to be restrictions this  year so our uh jamal stevenson our  college director and a lot of our scouts  uh did a lot on all 19 tape on these  guys because we didn't even know if  there was going to be a season in 20 for  a lot of these  schools and especially the power 5 but  then the power 5  came back alive and they did have a uh  they did have a season but then you know  you're watching the kid play in 19 and  why didn't he play as good in 2020 i  don't you know the dynamics on were they  able to work out at school weren't they  able to work out at school what were  they dealing with covet you know so  there's so many  variables that you see some of these  kids that played in 19 said wow he  didn't play very good in 20. but then he  saw a couple kids that popped up and  said yeah he he took another step  forward in 20. so  evaluating this year is really going to  be a a two-year pitcher of what you're  seeing in 19 and what you're seeing in  20 and then you're going to have to kind  of blend that together and come up with  uh what you think that player is you  mentioned yesterday  virtual interviews per player  is that is that unlimited number of  players and what's the time limit for  each of the five interviews you can do  yeah you're allowed up to five you're  allowed one hour per interview um you  know we've had we already started like  most teams have i sat on two or three  yesterday  um just to listen in as as the coaches  talk to the kids um  we uh  it'll be uh you're allowed to have an  unlimited amount of interviews i mean up  to five per player that's it but  unlimited amount of players that you can  interview you can interview 5 000 if you  want to  but strategically we have a plan in  place on who we want to interview  like i said there was a big uh big help  going down to the senior bowl and  knocking out 128 interviews so now the  coaches can piggyback off that but uh  and the other thing is i know you know  during these pro days there's going to  be no private workouts no dinners no  things like that you're at the school  you're doing the work uh you're  following the rules of the university as  far as the covet protocol the state and  local government protocol the nfl  protocol but at least we're out there  and able to get uh get our hands and and  not so much our hands on these guys i  shouldn't say that but just get out  there and see them in person no matter  how much you're able to do anything  always crap shoot first round's a crap  shoot the vikings have seen over the  years at the receiver position one good  one bad one good one badge you hit a  grand slam home run with 